080 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7112" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157080 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the orthogonal basis $\\mathcal{B}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^3$ and the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ below, find the value of $x_2,$ the second component of $[\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}}.$\n![](images/4f/4f788e589f34c94ac03e11f7cee87f9af695af2a86d57a2e4630f07c30babb1e.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157080 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5f10a215-83bb-545a-a0e1-ce702f773e6d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157080 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's denote the vectors of $\\mathcal{B}$ as $\\mathbf{q}_1,\\, \\mathbf{q}_2,\\,\\mathbf{q}_3.$ \n\nSince $\\mathcal{B}$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that ![](images/cf/cfa33ba159e0627ec7a7288e44249acd88e0037e285fa786888dfcc13e5d538c.png) where $x_i = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{x} \\cdot \\mathbf{q}_i}{\\mathbf{q}_i \\cdot \\mathbf{q}_i}.$ \n\nComputing $x_2,$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{2}}{{q}_{2}\\cdot {q}_{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 1+6\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot (-4)}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4+6+8}{1+1+16} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157081 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7113" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157081 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the **orthonormal** basis ![](images/5a/5a56202f818d8b8d10dd06d5e4bd02ee0aabc2f16758ca64cb6dc416fb71075c.png) of $\\mathbb R^2,$ find $[\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}}$ if ![](images/d9/d97e5bc94afc05532528354b82231eab87ca49ec72bd42879759c64c4165837d.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157081 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d7df79a9-2489-5fed-9e00-29890bd01f82" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157081 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's denote the vectors of $\\mathcal{B}$ as $\\mathbf{q}_1,\\, \\mathbf{q}_2.$ \n\nSince $\\mathcal{B}$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that ![](images/1b/1ba0b151abea3c5b1a050c6ff924f3718fcb045b063b1b47df7a73f9d15316c9.png) where $x_i = \\mathbf{x} \\cdot \\mathbf{q}_i.$ Computing the components of $\\mathbf{x},$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]=-2-6=-8 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]=-4+3=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have ![](images/51/51184680e9ec8b56a437334ca2a9281b1b364da2c35922839be13e545d92cec4.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157276 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048762 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157276 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049811 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157276 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050394 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157276 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186157768 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157276 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186157771 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157276 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186237889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157276 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186237890 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157276 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186237891 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157276 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186237893 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157276 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186326837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157276 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186351219 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157276 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186351220 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157276 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186351221 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157276 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186351233 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157276 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186373463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157276 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186375425 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157276 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding a Component of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthogonal Basis" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157276 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186157080 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157276 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "15b92bed-c97